  "scientific_question": "Do donors with more CA1 pyramidal neurons in reactive-astrocyte neighborhoods that lack nearby oligodendrocytes show faster memory decline beyond the current CA1 neuron-loss and reactive-niche panel?",
  "approach": "Assign cells to CA1, then identify CA1 Pyramidal Neuron, Reactive Astrocyte, and Oligodendrocyte labels. For each CA1 pyramidal neuron, query CA1 neighbors within radius r using centroid distance, excluding the focal cell. Mark the neuron as reactive-exposed if it has at least one Reactive Astrocyte neighbor. The donor biomarker is the fraction of reactive-exposed CA1 pyramidal neurons that have zero Oligodendrocyte neighbors within the same radius. If a donor has CA1 pyramidal neurons but none are reactive-exposed, return 0.0; if CA1 pyramidal neurons are absent, return NaN.",
  "variations": [
    {
      "name": "candidate_variant_a",
      "description": "Baseline local niche: fraction of reactive-exposed CA1 pyramidal neurons with zero oligodendrocyte neighbors within 60 px (~30 \u00b5m)."
    },
    {
      "name": "candidate_variant_b",
      "description": "Slightly broader local niche: same feature using an 80 px (~40 \u00b5m) radius."
    }
  ],
  "baseline_variation": "candidate_variant_a",
  "notes": "Use SegmentationNode/centroids for neighbor queries, ClassificationNode labels for cell types, and CustomAnnotations polygons for CA1 assignment; divide annotation polygon coordinates by 16 before region assignment. Restrict both focal cells and neighbors to CA1. Exclude self from neighbor counts. This is a centroid-only feature, so contour handling is not required for the score itself.",
  "rationale": "Recent rounds consistently improved the panel by sharpening a CA1 reactive astrocyte\u2013pyramidal injury niche, and round 7 showed that pyramidal atrophy inside that niche was especially informative. The next nonredundant step is to test whether those same stressed neuronal neighborhoods are also locally depleted of oligodendrocytes, adding a myelin/support-cell axis that is not yet represented and could outperform a weaker local-composition term."
